-# QEMU with a control menu in the SDL window
+# QEMU with a faster SDL display for desktop VMs
 
-QEMU master with a menu bar inside the SDL display window, in the spirit of
-[xemu](https://github.com/xemu-project/xemu): power, pause, snapshots, USB
-passthrough, usage statistics and VM information, without giving up the fast
-SDL + OpenGL display. It also makes the SDL display follow the host monitor's
-refresh rate.
+QEMU master with work on the SDL + OpenGL display and virtio-gpu for desktop
+guests: the display follows the host monitor's refresh rate, measures its
+frames, shares the clipboard, and passes the guest's buffers to the host
+without copies where it can.
 
 This is a fork of [QEMU](https://www.qemu.org): upstream master plus a few
-commits. The menu needs a Linux host.
+commits. An earlier version had a control menu (Dear ImGui) in the SDL
+window; it was removed in October 2026, since the VM manager app now does
+power, snapshots and USB passthrough.
 
